<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · song</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ya Rayah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1973">1973</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as يا رايح, Yâ râyiḥ</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">&quot;Ya <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reaya">Rayah</a>&quot; (&quot;you, the one leaving&quot;) is an Algerian chaâbi song written and performed in 1973 by Dahmane El Harrachi, whose name was Amrani Abderrahmane. It belongs to the chaâbi and Andalusian tradition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. It is a ballad of the traveller and the exile, of the emigrant and the longing to come back, and that theme has given it a wide appeal.</p></div>
